{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/622019-six-compacts-and-conspiracies-from-the-edo-jidai","id":622019,"title":"Six Compacts and Conspiracies from the Edo Jidai","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-10T04:00:17-07:00","id":622019,"title":"Six Compacts and Conspiracies from the Edo Jidai","content":"So, a while ago, I shared the Otodo. I said there were going to be five total Compacts and Conspiracies in the Dark Eras Edo Jidai content. <br /> <br /> I lied. <br /> <br /> There's six. A couple of people requested Miko for a group. We love Miko. So, we added one. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1UkJgf3IjdQuKvHmX_OxL6uBjCt02go-knYZ0Pc_UMVE/edit?usp=sharing\ufeff\" target=\"_blank\">Here they are</a>. <br /> <br /> I'll be putting them on the blog probably tomorrow, but we try to avoid blog posts on Mondays, because of the Monday Meeting Notes. And frankly, I figured I'd forget. <br /> <br /> So yeah. Six groups. Enjoy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T05:08:26-07:00","id":622063,"title":"","content":"If I may make a suggestion, I would change Setto so the Hototogisu must make a bargain (or more likely a scam) with the creature in order to take its power. The deal could be sealed with a shake of hands (the moment is transfered). I found this way more fitting for a merchant conspiracy. <br /> Alternatively the Hototogisu character may directly steal Dread Powers by force, but with a penalty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T05:29:33-07:00","id":622075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/622019-six-compacts-and-conspiracies-from-the-edo-jidai?p=622063#post622063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I may make a suggestion, I would change Setto so the Hototogisu must make a bargain (or more likely a scam) with the creature in order to take its power. The deal could be sealed with a shake of hands (the moment is transfered). I found this way more fitting for a merchant conspiracy.<br /> Alternatively the Hototogisu character may directly steal Dread Powers by force, but with a penalty.</div> </div> </div> </div>FWIW, they are very much thieves. They can deal in mortal wares as merchants, but their supernatural gift is a cuckoo's gift.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T05:50:32-07:00","id":622083,"title":"","content":"Is there any particular reason they're thieves? I ask because I concur with Raistlin. It just seems more fun to scam a monster than to sneak up and touch it.<br /> <br /> I think I might do a full &quot;Where I Read&quot; for this. It was fun doing it for Mortal Remains. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T05:57:22-07:00","id":622089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/622019-six-compacts-and-conspiracies-from-the-edo-jidai?p=622083#post622083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any particular reason they're thieves? I ask because I concur with Raistlin. It just seems more fun to scam a monster than to sneak up and touch it.<br /> <br /> I think I might do a full &quot;Where I Read&quot; for this. It was fun doing it for Mortal Remains. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. There is. It goes a little beyond the scope of this particular book, but yes.<br /> <br /> And if you do, I'll definitely read it. The whole thing is smaller than a single Mortal Remains chapter. But I think we fit a kind of remarkable amount of content into a small space.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T06:03:40-07:00","id":622092,"title":"","content":"&quot;This book&quot; so some other WoD book... This is Mage's metaphysics colonising other gamelines again isn't it!<br /> <br /> I kid <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> but if you get a chance, I am curious to the reasons.<br /> <br /> <br /> When I said &quot;I think&quot;, I was just being British. It meant I am going too; I'm planning to start this evening. I hope you enjoy reading it and feel free to comment along <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 08-10-2015, 09:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T06:10:56-07:00","id":622100,"title":"","content":"(Actually, I may do it via Social Manoeuvring; if you remove a final Door, you're eligible for theft.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T06:14:08-07:00","id":622104,"title":"","content":"Oooh. I like that idea a lot <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T06:16:22-07:00","id":622107,"title":"","content":"Updated version of Setto, as reflected in the Google Doc text:<br /> <br /> The Hototogisu take their name from a breed of cuckoo. They chose this, because their gift allows them to steal the mystical abilities of their marks. They call this Setto, which is literally theft or larceny. The Endowment is relatively new, as the Conspiracy only recently formalized.<br /> <br /> Setto is a one to five dot Merit. Each dot allows the Hototogisu a \u201cslot\u201d for a stolen Dread Power (or at Storyteller discretion, a Discipline, Gift, spell, Contract, or other activated monster ability if you\u2019re using other game lines). She cannot have a Dread Power above her total dots (so, with three dots, she can only steal a three dot Dread Power), and every dot rating allows exactly one Dread Power at that level or lower. So, for example, a character with four dots in Setto might have at most a four-dot power, a three dot, a two dot, and a one dot. She could never have two four-dot abilities. She can fill a slot with a lower-level Dread Power, however.<br /> <br /> <i>Stealing an ability requires the Hototogisu con her mark. As cutthroat merchants, this usually takes the part of a business transaction with a great deal of fast-talking, seduction, or blackmail. This is represented by a Social Maneuvering action; success means removing the victim\u2019s final Door.</i> It also necessitates your character to be aware of the ability. This may be by having seen it in action, or heard detailed accountings of its use. Spend a point of Willpower. Roll Intelligence + Larceny, penalized by the dot rating of the Dread Power in question. If successful, the Hototogisu steals the Dread Power. So long as the Hototogisu lives, and keeps the power, the monster is denied the ability completely. A Hototogisu can shed a power stolen with Setto at any time; the monster immediately regains the ability.<br /> <br /> To activate a stolen Dread Power, the Hototogisu must spend the normal Willpower cost for the Dread Power, and makes the same roll. Work with the Storyteller to determine how certain more complex Dread Powers interact with the hunter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":70,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","user":"MachineIV","date":". 08-10-2015, 09:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T06:34:05-07:00","id":622143,"title":"","content":"If I may be permitted to be pedantic for a moment.<br /> <br /> The wording in this section feels off to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/622019-six-compacts-and-conspiracies-from-the-edo-jidai?p=622107#post622107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As cutthroat merchants, this usually takes the part of a business transaction with a great deal of fast-talking, seduction, or blackmail. This is represented by a Social Maneuvering action; success means removing the victim\u2019s final Door.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;success means removing the victim\u2019s final Door.&quot; feels like you're saying some kind of special Social Manoeuvring roll that jumps to the final door. Something like &quot;after opening their final door, the victim's powers are ripe for taking&quot; would be clearer.<br /> <br /> <br /> This also gives me an thought. The current Social Manoeuvring rules work great for a week long negotiation over 3 ships worth of silk. But for smaller stuff, where you walk into a shop and haggle over a single outfit, and maybe leave without your Dread Power - barring an unlikely perfect impression - social manoeuvring mechanically doesn't fit that time frame.<br /> <br /> Perhaps when the 2E corebook comes out it should mention that if both parties are trying Social Manoeuvring simultaneously on each other such as haggling the timeframe can be accelerated.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: that small point aside. I do think this is a great improvement <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 08-10-2015, 09:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T06:41:22-07:00","id":622155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/622019-six-compacts-and-conspiracies-from-the-edo-jidai?p=622143#post622143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I may be permitted to be pedantic for a moment.<br /> <br /> The wording in this section feels off to me.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;success means removing the victim\u2019s final Door.&quot; feels like you're saying some kind of special Social Manoeuvring roll that jumps to the final door. Something like &quot;after opening their final door, the victim's powers are ripe for taking&quot; would be clearer.<br /> <br /> <br /> This also gives me an thought. The current Social Manoeuvring rules work great for a week long negotiation over 3 ships worth of silk. But for smaller stuff, where you walk into a shop and haggle over a single outfit, and maybe leave without your Dread Power - barring an unlikely perfect impression - social manoeuvring mechanically doesn't fit that time frame.<br /> <br /> Perhaps when the 2E corebook comes out it should mention that if both parties are trying Social Manoeuvring simultaneously on each other such as haggling the timeframe can be accelerated.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: that small point aside. I do think this is a great improvement <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Let's try this: <br /> <br /> Stealing an ability requires the Hototogisu con her mark. It also necessitates your character to be aware of the ability. This may be by having seen it in action, or heard detailed accountings of its use. As cutthroat merchants, this con usually takes the part of a business transaction with a great deal of fast-talking, seduction, or blackmail. This is occurs during a normal Social Maneuvering action; once the victim is down his final Door, you may attempt the theft with Setto (in addition to the normal effects of the successful Social Maneuvering action). Spend a point of Willpower. Roll Intelligence + Larceny, penalized by the dot rating of the Dread Power in question. If successful, the Hototogisu steals the Dread Power. So long as the Hototogisu lives, and keeps the power, the monster is denied the ability completely. A Hototogisu can shed a power stolen with Setto at any time; the monster immediately regains the ability. <br /> <br /> Re: Manoeuvring, is that your common experience? Usually with slight manipulation, in my games most Manoeuvring is at the hour intervals, or even perfect impressions. Maybe my players like to edge in for the kill, but that's been most of my experiences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T06:50:53-07:00","id":622168,"title":"","content":"I won't speak for The King's Raven, but in my games if someone can't get what they want out of their first interaction via the social manoeuvring system, it generally doesn't happen that session. It has a tendency to then get forgotten about or relegated to side things between games or at the next game (if they remember). I will be honest though - the rules for the system stymied the heck out of me for months. That probably didn't help me run games with them.<br /> <br /> I am psyched about these compacts though. They're gonna be so much fun. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1462,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","user":"Xenesis","date":". 08-10-2015, 10:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T06:59:47-07:00","id":622177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/622019-six-compacts-and-conspiracies-from-the-edo-jidai?p=622155#post622155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stealing an ability requires the Hototogisu con her mark. It also necessitates your character to be aware of the ability. This may be by having seen it in action, or heard detailed accountings of its use. As cutthroat merchants, this con usually takes the part of a business transaction with a great deal of fast-talking, seduction, or blackmail. This is occurs during a normal Social Maneuvering action; once the victim is down his final Door, you may attempt the theft with Setto (in addition to the normal effects of the successful Social Maneuvering action). Spend a point of Willpower. Roll Intelligence + Larceny, penalized by the dot rating of the Dread Power in question. If successful, the Hototogisu steals the Dread Power. So long as the Hototogisu lives, and keeps the power, the monster is denied the ability completely. A Hototogisu can shed a power stolen with Setto at any time; the monster immediately regains the ability.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thumbs up! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/622019-six-compacts-and-conspiracies-from-the-edo-jidai?p=622155#post622155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re: Manoeuvring, is that your common experience? Usually with slight manipulation, in my games most Manoeuvring is at the hour intervals, or even perfect impressions. Maybe my players like to edge in for the kill, but that's been most of my experiences.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cards on the table. I was going by my experiences of roleplaying shopping at a Goblin Market, not my experience using the Social Manoeuvring rules.<br /> <br /> Shopping at a Goblin Market was the only time I've haggled in play. It was actually pure role play, the only thing I brought that had an effect on the game beyond pure flavour and the joy of roleplaying shopping at the Market; were goblin contracts and we treated the exp prices of those as non-negotiable.<br /> <br /> So When I talked about the timeframe for Manoeuvring I was trying to imagine how the haggling I did at the Market would have worked if we had used the Manoeuvring rules. I couldn't justify saying perfect impressions, because what smart Changeling trusts a Goblin Marketeer? but at the same time; it was over in a couple of minuets at the most.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T07:05:57-07:00","id":622197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/622019-six-compacts-and-conspiracies-from-the-edo-jidai?p=622177#post622177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thumbs up! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Cards on the table. I was going by my experiences of roleplaying shopping at a Goblin Market, not my experience using the Social Manoeuvring rules.<br /> <br /> Shopping at a Goblin Market was the only time I've haggled in play. It was actually pure role play, the only thing I brought that had an effect on the game beyond pure flavour and the joy of roleplaying shopping at the Market; were goblin contracts and we treated the exp prices of those as non-negotiable.<br /> <br /> So When I talked about the timeframe for Manoeuvring I was trying to imagine how the haggling I did at the Market would have worked if we had used the Manoeuvring rules. I couldn't justify saying perfect impressions, because what smart Changeling trusts a Goblin Marketeer? but at the same time; it was over in a couple of minuets at the most.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh sure sure. I think that if someone were playing Hototogisu, they'd quickly learn how to nail that perfect impression. Personally, and this is just my own style, but I'd eat that up. I'd quickly figure out exactly how my character milks impressions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T07:23:05-07:00","id":622230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So long as the Hototogisu lives, and keeps the power, the monster is denied the ability completely. A Hototogisu can shed a power stolen with Setto at any time; the monster immediately regains the ability </div> </div> </div>And if is the monster the one who dies first?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T07:25:07-07:00","id":622233,"title":"","content":"Sure, I could definitely see myself playing a con-artist type who milks impressions for all they're worth <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> . I can also see myself playing a charchter who's chief weapon in anonymity (after all, you don't want monsters coming back for their powers) and thus avoids giving a strong impression. It depends what mood I'm in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T07:25:29-07:00","id":622234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/622019-six-compacts-and-conspiracies-from-the-edo-jidai?p=622230#post622230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And if is the monster the one who dies first?</div> </div> </div> </div>Then the Hototogisu keeps it, until she decides she wants to free up the slot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T07:44:52-07:00","id":622250,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Malleus Maleficarum:</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> They may have the best of intentions, but their methods do not work here. They embolden sleeping dragons, and make our work harder.<br /> <br /> I was wondering when this shoe would drop. Knowing the Church's history in Japan. </span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T07:49:58-07:00","id":622253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/622019-six-compacts-and-conspiracies-from-the-edo-jidai?p=622250#post622250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Malleus Maleficarum:</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> They may have the best of intentions, but their methods do not work here. They embolden sleeping dragons, and make our work harder.<br /> <br /> I was wondering when this shoe would drop. Knowing the Church's history in Japan. </span></span><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>For a little more on the Malleus, here's their remaining treatment: <br /> <br /> <b>The Malleus Maleficarum</b> barely survive in Tokugawa\u2019s Nihon. A couple of members struggle to survive, as their faith is publicly outlawed. Three straggling members maintain a single cell in Dejima, under the auspices of the Dutch traders. They have to be very careful not to display any signs of their faith. While unknown to the public, they are well-known to those on the Vigil; their existence remains as controversial. The Otodo maintain a healthy suspicion of the remaining Malleus, as the Conspiracy once declared the Otodo demonic, and deserving of destruction. Gimu look to the Malleus as a cancer that needs to be removed from Nihon, before it infects ambitious daimyo. However, bringing down political forces would risk revealing their own illegal Vigil. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T08:01:40-07:00","id":622258,"title":"","content":"wait- when did that happened? how did I missed this thread? gonna read everything right now!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T08:07:10-07:00","id":622260,"title":"","content":"But for what I know, Malleus Maleficrum were catholics, and dutchs were calvinists. So, I don't see them under the auspices of dutchs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T09:02:19-07:00","id":622337,"title":"","content":"so after a first read, here is what I have to say-<br /> <br /> The Ama San are very interesting. Personally, I find ancient Japan as one of the more interesting civilizations I've read about, so I am always happy to learn new information about it. While I knew that pearl divers were a feature of Japan's culture, I didn't knew it was a feminine job, so that's a bonus. The main thing which interest me about that group is that the Vigil looks like a a reaction to their profession instead of their defining trait- they are pearl divers, first and foremost, hunters later. Also, all the Whale Whistle thingy sounds really cool.<br /> <br /> The Azusa Miko seem to be an example for a supernatural compact, which shows how a group can have supernatural powers without having access to a defined Endowment. I kinda hoped for them to be a Conspiracy, but compact works better for them, especially in that Era. In general I've always liked the Miko, so a group based around them sounds really cool. Maybe they are a potential Conspiracy, maybe they are a dying one, maybe they'll never be and maybe they'll just go extinct- in sort, there are so many potential futures I can see for that group, and they are really compelling to play.<br /> <br /> I must say that I'm a bit disappointing about the Bijin. If I remember correctly, they were originally described as a &quot;male escorts compact&quot;, but it seems that they also include women in them. The reason I feel that way is that there are 2 different mostly women groups, and I've hoped that they would balance it a bit. I mean, as a male, I kinda want an whole male group because it seems that the only &quot;one gender&quot; groups presented are women- the Maiden Blood, Ama and Miko. I understand from where it may come from, but it still kinda bugs me. Other than that, they are really good and interesting.<br /> <br /> I don't usually like samurais, but the Gimu seem to be an exception- the fact that they focus more around the &quot;warrior nobles&quot; part and less about the &quot;swordsmen with awesome swords&quot; is a really nice twist. The whole honor thing still annoys me, but this is a personal dislike and an integral part of being a samurai. <br /> <br /> The Hototogisu are everything I wanted and more- thieves and merchants who steal the powers of their enemies? cool. They feel like something the modern Cheiron Group would have to deal with, for better or worse.They are just the type of bastards I like to play, and their Endowments is just awesome. In sort, they are one of the best groups in Hunter, IMO.<br /> <br /> and I already said that the Otodo are awesome in their own thread.<br /> <br /> In sort, can't wait for the book! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T09:11:04-07:00","id":622346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uxas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/622019-six-compacts-and-conspiracies-from-the-edo-jidai?p=622260#post622260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But for what I know, Malleus Maleficrum were catholics, and dutchs were calvinists. So, I don't see them under the auspices of dutchs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll make it clear in the final draft that they are not operating openly; they're doing their work covertly. The Dutch actively fought back the Christians, and that's one of the main reasons they were allowed to trade. These Malleus are not openly religious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T09:13:03-07:00","id":622347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/622019-six-compacts-and-conspiracies-from-the-edo-jidai?p=622337#post622337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I must say that I'm a bit disappointing about the Bijin. If I remember correctly, they were originally described as a &quot;male escorts compact&quot;, but it seems that they also include women in them. The reason I feel that way is that there are 2 different mostly women groups, and I've hoped that they would balance it a bit. I mean, as a male, I kinda want an whole male group because it seems that the only &quot;one gender&quot; groups presented are women- the Maiden Blood, Ama and Miko. I understand from where it may come from, but it still kinda bugs me. Other than that, they are really good and interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>For whatever it's worth, this came from talking to some locals about the history. We felt from these discussions that the men and women entertainers/escorts were just too intertwined to keep separate as a group. The gender segregation just wasn't what it'd need to be to have a gender-specific group. I totally feel your point, and considered it quite a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T09:25:05-07:00","id":622352,"title":"","content":"For what it's worth. I was thinking similar thoughts to LostLight; but IMO real history takes precedence.<br /> <br /> There'll always be another book where the balance can be redressed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T10:03:40-07:00","id":622381,"title":"","content":"Eh - in a patriarchal society, there's less call for an &quot;all male groups&quot;. The social norm in society is under male dominance - all female groups are more called for as a response to that.<br /> <br /> That said, in a historic setting, it would be completely believable to have a given Compact who are a military force be all male (with noted female exceptions).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T10:51:15-07:00","id":622421,"title":"","content":"Speak for yourself. I live in a matriarchy.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://www.breakingnews.ie/media/images/z/zzzQueenOnIronThrone_large.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T11:04:10-07:00","id":622449,"title":"","content":"I was referring to Edo Japan.<br /> <br /> Though on the topic of female heads of state, give me 2 years to respond to that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T12:30:22-07:00","id":622546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/622019-six-compacts-and-conspiracies-from-the-edo-jidai?p=622449#post622449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though on the topic of female heads of state, give me 2 years to respond to that.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're going to take down the Queen, I would highly advise not doing it. She's lived through the Blitz and can shoot with the best of them.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T12:33:24-07:00","id":622549,"title":"","content":"I always knew you believed in the patriarchy Glamourweaver, but to take it so far... if you want to get to Her Majesty you'll have to go through me first.<br /> <br /> (More seriously. I wouldn't say the norm for Edo Japan hunters is automatically male dominated because Hunters violate social norms by definition. Gender norm are far less powerful than the don't talk about monster norm. Unless the text explicitly says otherwise I'll assume they're egalitarian.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 08-10-2015, 03:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T13:02:04-07:00","id":622580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/622019-six-compacts-and-conspiracies-from-the-edo-jidai?p=622253#post622253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For a little more on the Malleus, here's their remaining treatment:<br /> <br /> <b>The Malleus Maleficarum</b> barely survive in Tokugawa\u2019s Nihon. A couple of members struggle to survive, as their faith is publicly outlawed. Three straggling members maintain a single cell in Dejima, under the auspices of the Dutch traders. They have to be very careful not to display any signs of their faith. While unknown to the public, they are well-known to those on the Vigil; their existence remains as controversial. The Otodo maintain a healthy suspicion of the remaining Malleus, as the Conspiracy once declared the Otodo demonic, and deserving of destruction. Gimu look to the Malleus as a cancer that needs to be removed from Nihon, before it infects ambitious daimyo. However, bringing down political forces would risk revealing their own illegal Vigil.</div> </div> </div> </div>Something worth looking at is the <i>kakure kirishitan</i><br /> <br /> <i><b>Kakure Kirishitan</b> (\u96a0\u308c\u30ad\u30ea\u30b7\u30bf\u30f3<sup><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:Installing_Japanese_character_sets\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#00e\">?</span></a></sup>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japanese_language\" target=\"_blank\">Japanese</a> for &quot;Hidden Christian&quot;) is a modern term for a member of the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japan\" target=\"_blank\">Japanese</a> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Catholic_Church\" target=\"_blank\">Catholic Church</a> during the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Edo_period\" target=\"_blank\">Edo period</a> that went underground after the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shimabara_Rebellion\" target=\"_blank\">Shimabara Rebellion</a> in the 1630s.<sup><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kakure_Kirishitan#cite_note-enc-1\" target=\"_blank\">[1]</a></sup><sup><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kakure_Kirishitan#cite_note-d-2\" target=\"_blank\">[2]</a></sup> After the start of the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sakoku\" target=\"_blank\">Sakoku</a> period in 1639, it was officially prohibited from teaching the European <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Catholic\" target=\"_blank\">Catholic</a> religion.</i><br /> <br /> It didn't fall completely apart and the Malleus may have more cells in Japan than one would expect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T13:52:00-07:00","id":622617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/622019-six-compacts-and-conspiracies-from-the-edo-jidai?p=622347#post622347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For whatever it's worth, this came from talking to some locals about the history. We felt from these discussions that the men and women entertainers/escorts were just too intertwined to keep separate as a group. The gender segregation just wasn't what it'd need to be to have a gender-specific group. I totally feel your point, and considered it quite a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>well, if the reason is historical, I can accept that. Again, the group is cool, all in all, it was just that they are not what I've expected for. <br /> <br /> considering that I have some strong opinions about all the &quot;patriarchy&quot; thing, and I don't want to ruin the thread, I would keep them to myself and hope that one day, we will get an &quot;all male&quot; group, even if it is just to feel that there is a reason for the &quot;all female&quot; groups to exist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T13:59:44-07:00","id":622623,"title":"","content":"You know LostLight, you're probably a more prolific Hunter fanwriter than me at this point <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (Yes I know it's not the same as cannon)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"